<title>USA: Metal Recovery picks designer for plant.</title>
<headline>Metal Recovery picks designer for plant.</headline>
<dateline>EAST CHICAGO, Ind. 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Metal Recovery Technologies Inc said Monday it selected Toledo, Ohio-based SSOE Inc to design and engineer a 250,000-ton-per-year dezincing plant proposed for General Motors Corp.</p>
<p>To defer costs, Metal Recovery will pay SSOE with stock purchase warrants and grant monies from the Department of Energy.</p>
<p>On February 25, Metal Recovery said that GM requested a detailed proposal for a dezincing facility. When built, the plant will yield about $35 million worth of reusable &quot;black&quot; scrap and $6.5 million worth of zinc powder per year.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
